The '''Disaster of Sweden''' ({{langx|es|Desastre de Suecia}})<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.elgrafico.com.ar/coberturas-historicas/1958-el-desastre-de-suecia.php |title=No es cuestión de hombres |access-date=8 January 2024|date=20 June 1958 |work=El Gráfico|language=es|archive-date=6 April 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150406010815/http://www.elgrafico.com.ar/coberturas-historicas/1958-el-desastre-de-suecia.php |url-status=dead }}</ref> is the name given to the early elimination of the [[Argentina national football team|Argentina football team]] from the [[1958 FIFA World Cup]] at the hands of the [[Czechoslovakia national football team|Czechoslovakia football team]]. The match was played on 15 June 1958, at the [[Olympia (Helsingborg)|Olympiastadion]] in the city of [[Helsingborg]], Sweden, the host country of the championship. That day, Czechoslovakia beat Argentina 6–1. The final result means the heaviest defeat for the Albiceleste team in a FIFA World Cup.<ref>https://www.infobae.com/deportes-2/mundial-2018/2018/06/15/a-60-anos-del-desastre-de-suecia-el-recuerdo-de-la-peor-derrota-de-argentina-en-mundiales/ ''A 60 años del "desastre de Suecia": el recuerdo de la peor derrota de Argentina en Mundiales''. Infobae, 3 July 2018.</ref><ref>https://www.elgrafico.com.ar/articulo/las-cronicas-de-el-grafico/31835/1958-era-pan-comido-fue-desastre 1958. ERA PAN COMIDO, FUE DESASTRE. El Gráfico, 14 May 2018.</ref>

==Background==
Before that meeting, the two teams had only met once, on 16 August 1956, at [[Estadio Gasómetro|El Gasómetro]] in Buenos Aires with a 1–0 victory for the locals.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.livefutbol.com/cronica/freundschaft-1956-august-argentinien-cssr/ | title=Argentina - Checoslovaquia 1:0 (Amistosos Internacionales 1956, Agosto) }}</ref><ref>https://www.promiedos.com.ar/historialsel.php?equipo1=785&equipo2=1041&modo=todos Promiedos.com Historial completo de Argentina vs. Checoslovaquia</ref>

Argentina arrived at the World Cup with the title of South American champion in tow, after the achievement obtained [[1957 South American Championship|a year earlier in Peru]]. Many of the Argentinian football figures of that time, such as [[Amadeo Carrizo]], [[Ángel Labruna]] (both members of [[Club Atlético River Plate|River's]] [[La Maquina]]), [[Oreste Corbatta|Omar Corbatta]], [[José Ramos Delgado]] (who later played alongside [[Pelé]] in [[Santos FC|Santos]]) and [[José Sanfilippo]] (historic goalscorer of [[San Lorenzo de Almagro]]) took place in the final squad that traveled to Sweden in search of the first world conquest of the Argentinian team and after 24 years of absence from the biggest event.<ref name=infobae>{{cite web |url=https://www.infobae.com/2012/06/14/653468-argentina-sufria-la-peor-derrota-un-mundial-el-desastre-suecia-1958/ |title=Argentina sufría la peor derrota en un Mundial: "El desastre de Suecia 1958" |access-date=8 January 2024|date=13 November 2017|publisher=Infobae|language=es|archive-date=8 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240108193732/https://www.infobae.com/2012/06/14/653468-argentina-sufria-la-peor-derrota-un-mundial-el-desastre-suecia-1958/ |url-status=live }}</ref> With [[Guillermo Stábile]] as coach, the Argentinian team [[1958 FIFA World Cup qualification (CONMEBOL)|reached qualification]] after eliminating [[Bolivia national football team|Bolivia]] and [[Chile national football team|Chile]].

Czechoslovakia, for its part, [[1958 FIFA World Cup qualification (UEFA)|had qualified in UEFA group 4]] beating [[Wales national football team|Wales]] and [[East Germany national football team|East Germany]]. As at that time there was still no official football championship between all the European teams (the [[UEFA European Championship|UEFA Euro]] only began in 1960), the only rivals arose from the friendlies determined by [[FIFA]], and from the [[Central European International Cup]], a tournament which was played between the late '20s and '50s by the strongest teams in said continental region. The Czechoslovak team entered the World Cup with 7 consecutive matches without defeat, 2 of them friendlies, 3 in the qualifying round and 2 in the Central European Cup.

==The World Cup in Sweden==
In 1958, both teams met in Group A of the World Cup with [[Germany national football team|West Germany]] and [[Northern Ireland national football team|Northern Ireland]].

After the dispute of the first two matches, Argentina arrived with 2 points as a result of a defeat against West Germany by 3-1 and a victory against the British team by the same score. Czechoslovakia, on the other hand, had achieved a single point due to a draw against the Germans and a narrow defeat against Northern Ireland, so they had to win to achieve a qualification attempt.

