==Consequences==
[[File:Varacka y labruna en vestuario suecia 1958.jpg|thumb|200px|José Varacka and Ángel Labruna after the match]]
The defeat, considered humiliating, brought immediate consequences and others that decisively influenced the subsequent development of [[Football in Argentina|Argentinian football]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.efdeportes.com/efd141/argentina-y-el-mundial-de-futbol-de-suecia-de-1958.htm |title=Argentina y el Mundial de Fútbol de Suecia de 1958, La otra historia (Primera parte) |access-date=8 January 2024|date=February 2010 |work=efdeportes|language=es|archive-date=8 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240108193731/http://www.efdeportes.com/efd141/argentina-y-el-mundial-de-futbol-de-suecia-de-1958.htm |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.efdeportes.com/efd142/argentina-y-el-mundial-de-futbol-de-suecia-de-1958-2.htm |title=Argentina y el Mundial de Fútbol de Suecia de 1958, La otra historia (Segunda parte) |access-date=8 January 2024|date=March 2010 |work=efdeportes|language=es|archive-date=16 December 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181216154529/http://www.efdeportes.com/efd142/argentina-y-el-mundial-de-futbol-de-suecia-de-1958-2.htm |url-status=live}}</ref>

The early elimination of the Argentinian team was echoed in the main graphic media of the time. Criticism began to fall on the president of the [[Argentine Football Association|AFA]], Raúl Colombo, and the coaching staff, while the team was received at the [[Ministro Pistarini International Airport|Ezeiza Airport]] with insults and throwing coins.<ref name=infobae /><ref>https://tn.com.ar/deportes/mundial/2022/09/29/el-desastre-de-suecia-por-que-argentina-tuvo-su-peor-mundial-en-1958/ ''El desastre de Suecia: por qué Argentina tuvo su peor Mundial en 1958.'' TN, 29 September 2022.</ref>

[[Guillermo Stábile]] resigned from the coach position after this episode, a position he had held since 1939 and in which he had achieved 6 [[Copa América|South American Championship]] titles.

[[Ángel Labruna]], forward of that team, later declared to the press:

{{blockquote|We went blindfolded, blind. We were not physically or tactically prepared to face 3 games in one week.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202306/631244-futbol-seleccionado-aniversario-desastre-mundial-suecia-58.html |title=La hora más dolorosa del seleccionado argentino en los Mundiales de fútbol |access-date=January 8, 2024|date=June 14, 2023|publisher=Télam |location=Buenos Aires |language=es|archive-date=January 8, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240108193704/https://www.telam.com.ar/notas/202306/631244-futbol-seleccionado-aniversario-desastre-mundial-suecia-58.html |url-status=live}}</ref>}}

[[Amadeo Carrizo]], the Argentinian goalkeeper, resigned from his country's national team, to which he returned, however, in 1964 for the [[Taça das Nações|Nations Cup]]. He would later reveal the following:

{{blockquote|When we arrived in the country, after the elimination, the plane had to land on a farm in [[Monte Grande]] so they wouldn't kill us. Some Argentinian journalists who were in Sweden had asked people to go look for us at the air station with sticks and stones. There was a lot of anger, they wanted to kill us, they said we were traitors. Nobody was going to believe us that Argentina lacked organization and that none of us charged a single peso to play in that World Cup.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.infobae.com/deportes-2/mundial-2018/2018/06/15/a-60-anos-del-desastre-de-suecia-el-recuerdo-de-la-peor-derrota-de-argentina-en-mundiales/ |title=A 60 años del "desastre de Suecia": el recuerdo de la peor derrota de Argentina en Mundiales |access-date=January 8, 2024 |last=Del Moral |first=Milton |date=June 15, 2018|publisher=Infobae|language=es|archive-date=January 8, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240108193705/https://www.infobae.com/deportes-2/mundial-2018/2018/06/15/a-60-anos-del-desastre-de-suecia-el-recuerdo-de-la-peor-derrota-de-argentina-en-mundiales/ |url-status=live}}</ref>}}

[[José Sanfilippo|Jose Sanfilippo]], who did not play in that match, later stated:

{{blockquote|We didn't even know what color our opponents' jerseys were, let alone how they played. It was a total mess, with lots of fights between the players and the coach. (...) It was a world of difference. They'd send a 40- or 50-meter pass right to a teammate's chest—it was a whole different level of speed; we looked like turtles. We learned a ton at that World Cup, because all we knew was to dribble.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Borinsky |first1=Diego |title=José Sanfilippo, 100x100: “Messi hasta es mejor que yo, este pibe pasó todos los límites” |url=https://www.elgrafico.com.ar/articulo/las-entrevistas-de-el-grafico/8118/jose-sanfilippo-100x100-messi-hasta-es-mejor-que-yo-este-pibe-paso-todos-los-limites |website=El gráfico |access-date=16 June 2026 |language=Spanish |date=3 June 2026}}</ref>}}

